# Error classes in their own files

Put every error class in a dedicated file whose name matches the exported type. Do not declare error classes in the same file as a port, adapter, use case, controller, or other primary type that throws or returns them.

Group those files in an `error` directory next to the module they belong to. Import the error type from that file wherever it is constructed or checked.

A base error and each specialized subclass are separate files. One public error class per file.
